<title>PORTUGAL: BTA to pay out 60 pct of 96 profit - paper.</title>
<headline>BTA to pay out 60 pct of 96 profit - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's Banco Totta &amp; Acores (BTA) expects to distribute 60 percent of its 1996 profits to shareholders, the bank's president Alipio Dias told Publico newspaper.</p>
<p>Dias declined to make a profit forecast but said that the result would be slightly better than in 1995.</p>
<p>Last year the bank posted consolidated net profit of 17.2 billion escudos on which it paid a net dividend of 168.63 escudos.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
